Hi Mike,

First of all, thanks a lot for putting this together. It's a great resource to learn and test the model :)

I am looking into the CONV_ecto function and I have a couple of doubts.

1) I think that the variables PR2 and SC2 (in lines 215 and 216 in github) are not being used, right? I guess those are coming from fortran, where variables are often renamed.

2) Using the default parameter values and the frog geometry, I realized that ANU is calculated twice. First in line 236 because GEOMETRY == 4 and RE is not > 40000 or <= 2000. And then it is overwritten in line 280, where a ANU value is computed regardless of the RE number value. Maybe the parameter combination is not realistic, and that's why this is happening, but I would like to understand which is the logic behind this.

Thank you so much!
All the best,
Urtzi

